  "title": "Emir Abd al-Qadir",
  "summary": "Abd al-Qadir, born near Mascara in a Sufi family, led some fifteen years of armed resistance to the French occupation of Algeria. Abandoned by followers and outlawed in Morocco, he surrendered in December 1847, was held in France until 1852, then settled in Damascus, where he died on 26 May 1883.",
